course: dictionary
lesson: 2341
title: One word, many crusts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word crust can mean the hard outside of bread, the base of a pie, a hard layer on something soft, or the thin rocky outside of the Earth. «Noah said sorry and asked for no crusts, and now he eats it all.» Here the crusts are on bread, because that is what people usually cut off.
explain: Now read «A fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks can slip.» Crust here is not bread at all. The words Earth's and rocks are your clues, so crust means the hard, rocky outer layer of the Earth. Always ask: what does this word mean in this sentence, and does my meaning still fit?
explain: «A volcano is an opening in the crust where melted rock, gas and ash escape from inside the Earth.» The clue is inside the Earth, which tells you that the crust is the outside layer that the melted rock must break through. When a word has several meanings, check the words next to it before you choose.
fact: A crust is the hard outer part of something.
fact: A bread crust is the hard outside of a loaf or slice of bread.
fact: The Earth's crust is the thin, rocky outer layer that we live on.
fact: A crust of ice is a hard layer on top of something soft, like snow.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is right: look at the words around it.
exercise: «Noah said sorry and asked for no crusts, and now he eats it all.» What are the crusts in this sentence? | The rocks under the ground | The sauce on top of a pizza | The middle soft part of the bread | *The hard outside edges of the bread
exercise: «A volcano is an opening in the crust where melted rock, gas and ash escape from inside the Earth.» What does crust mean here? | A hard outside layer of bread | A layer of frozen snow | *The thin, rocky outer layer of the Earth | A pastry base for a pie
exercise: «A fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks can slip.» Find and copy one word that means a split in rock. | Earth's | slip | *crack | rocks
test: A pizza ___ can be thin and crispy, or thick and chewy. | *crust | crumb | crater | cricket
test: After the rain froze, a thin ___ of ice covered the puddle. | crate | crowd | crumb | *crust
exam: «Eating crusts does not make hair curly; curliness comes mostly from your genes.» What does this sentence tell us? | Only pizza crusts can curl hair | Eating crusts makes hair grow faster | Crusts make hair curly | *Crusts do not change your hair; genes matter far more
